# pulse starter: api-and-worker ({{.Lang}})

A CRUD API with background jobs and persistence, entirely offline.
One small file per job:

```
services/create-order/   POST /orders        → save order + queue a job
services/get-order/      GET /orders/{id}    → read the order back
services/worker/         order-events queue  → mark the order processed
```

```
POST /orders ──▶ createOrder ──▶ orders table (status: pending)
                      └────────▶ order-events queue ──▶ worker ─▶ table (status: processed)
GET /orders/{id} ─▶ getOrder ──▶ orders table
```

Dependencies were installed automatically by `pulse init`{{if eq .Lang "python"}} (a project
`.venv` pulse finds on its own — no activation needed){{end}}. If that was skipped:

{{if eq .Lang "python"}}```bash
python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt
```{{else}}```bash
npm install
```{{end}}

The whole loop:

```bash
pulse start
curl -X POST localhost:3000/orders -d '{"sku":"A1","qty":2}'   # → 201, status "pending"
curl localhost:3000/orders/<that-id>                            # → status "processed" ✓
```

More to try: `pulse logs worker -f` (live logs) · `pulse send order-events
'{"id":"x"}'` (queue a job by hand) · the retry demo `curl -X POST
localhost:3000/orders -d '{"sku":"X","fail":true}'` (worker raises → 3
retries → dead-letter queue; watch `pulse list`) · stop and restart pulse —
data and queued jobs survive.

pulse points the vanilla AWS SDK at its local mocks via `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL`,
so this code runs unmodified in real AWS.

Prefer the other language? `pulse init <name> --template api-and-worker --lang node|python`
